      "slug": "alphabet-and-sounds",
      "title": "Alphabet and sounds",
      "shortExplanation": "Dominican Kwéyòl writing uses letters familiar from French-influenced Caribbean orthographies, with sounds that learners should practise carefully.",
      "examplesJson": "[{\"kweyol\":\"a\",\"english\":\"as in 'papa'\"},{\"kweyol\":\"é\",\"english\":\"a brighter vowel sound, as often taught in 'mèsi'\"},{\"kweyol\":\"ou\",\"english\":\"like 'oo' in 'food'\"}]",
      "commonMistakes": "Do not assume every letter sounds exactly like English or French in every word.",
      "practiceActivity": "Say bonjou, mèsi and dlo slowly. Tap each syllable, then listen again if audio is available.",
